/**
\fn void pdg::ElementRef::setLiveAttributes(const Attributes& attrs)
\brief Associate an element with a live Attributes or AnimatedAttributes source.

Rendering, bounds queries and hit tests read the source's current values. Multiple
elements may share one source. Geometry and control points remain unchanged.
The association follows the element when it is reordered; removed references never
retarget a different element. Calling setAttributes() replaces the association
with a copy. clearLiveAttributes() freezes its current sample.

The association retains its final values and image/font resources if the source
is destroyed or garbage collected. It does not retain or run the source's animation
schedule. Advance a standalone AnimatedAttributes with animate(deltaSeconds), once
per update regardless of how many elements share it or how often they are drawn.
Keep a reference to the source while you intend to edit or advance it.

Drawing snapshots serialize current values, not the association or its schedule.
getAttributes() continues to return an independent value snapshot.

\param attrs Source whose values the element should follow.

\par Example
\code{.cpp}
std::unique_ptr<pdg::Drawing> drawing(pdg::Drawing::create());
pdg::AnimatedAttributes<> style;
style.fillColor(pdg::Color(1.f, 0.f, 0.f));
std::unique_ptr<pdg::ElementRef> element(drawing->addRect(pdg::Rect(40, 40), style));
element->setLiveAttributes(style);
style.moveTo(100, 0, 1, pdg::linearTween);
style.animate(0.25); // All associated elements observe this sample.
\endcode
\see clearLiveAttributes(), hasLiveAttributes(), setAttributes(), getAttributes()
*/
/**
\fn void pdg::ElementRef::clearLiveAttributes()
\brief Freeze the current sample and release the association.
A removed or unassociated element is unchanged.
*/
/**
\fn bool pdg::ElementRef::hasLiveAttributes() const
\brief Test whether the element holds a live sample association.
\return True until clearing, replacement with setAttributes(), or removal,
including a frozen sample after source destruction.
*/
